<!-- Corporate Network Design project -->
<section>
  <h3>Corporate Network Design – Group Project</h3>

  <!-- Project image -->
  <img class="project-image" src="/images/corporate-network.jpeg"
     alt="Corporate Network Design topology">

  <!-- Project description -->
  <p>
    Worked with a partner to design and simulate a corporate network
    connecting three buildings using Cisco Packet Tracer.
    The project involved IPv4 addressing, subnetting, static routing,
    and testing network connectivity between buildings and an Internet server.
  </p>

  <!-- Downloadable project file -->
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/project-files/corporate-network.pkt" download>
   Download Project File
  </a>

</section>


<!-- Multi-Site Network Design project -->
<section>
  <h3>Multi-Site Network Design – Group Project</h3>

  <!-- Project image -->
  <img class="project-image" src="/images/multi-site-network.jpeg"
     alt="Multi-Site Corporate Network topology">

  <!-- Project description -->
  <p>
    Collaborated with a team of three to design and implement a
    corporate network connecting Toronto, Vancouver, Chicago, and
    Mexico using Cisco Packet Tracer.
    I was responsible for building the entire network topology,
    configuring the Vancouver and Chicago networks, and ensuring
    successful connectivity across all branches.
    The project involved VLANs, inter-VLAN routing, OSPF, BGP,
    and network connectivity testing.
  </p>

  <!-- Downloadable project file -->
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/project-files/multi-site-network.pkt" download>
    Download Project File
  </a>
</section>


<!-- Library Management System project -->
<section>
  <h3>Library Management System</h3>

  <!-- Project image -->
  <img class="project-image" src="/images/library-system.jpeg"
     alt="Library Management System program">

  <!-- Project description -->
  <p>
    A Python-based Library Management System that allows users to
    borrow, return, and manage books through a console interface.
    The project uses object-oriented programming concepts,
    including classes and inheritance, CSV file handling,
    exception handling, and overdue penalty calculations.
  </p>

  <!-- Downloadable project file -->
   <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/project-files/library-system.pdf" download>
      Download Project File
   </a>
</section>


<!-- Python Calculator project -->
<section>
  <h3>Simple Calculator Application – Python GUI</h3>

  <!-- Project image -->
  <img class="project-image" src="/images/calculator.jpeg"
     alt="Python calculator graphical interface">

  <!-- Project description -->
  <p>
    A simple calculator application using Python and PyQt5.
    The application features a graphical user interface that
    allows users to perform addition, subtraction,
    multiplication, and division.
    It also includes input fields, interactive buttons,
    and error handling for division by zero.
  </p>

